    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d19">

                <pb facs="0126" n="20" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg20"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr.
                            Grant</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-08-06"><hi rendition="#italic">August 6,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 133.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your dispatch No. 168, of the
                    15th ultimo, in relation to the case of Nikolaus Bader, the assisted emigrant,
                    you may address a dignified note to the foreign office in the sense you suggest,
                    saying, <pb facs="0127" n="21" xml:id="pg21"/> in conclusion, that, as Bader has
                    been returned, pursuant to the statutes of the United States, to the country
                    whence he was assisted to emigrate, the incident may be regarded as
                    terminated.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
